       - "2026-10-17: owner feedback: evenings looked about 5600 K next to the original (the vehicle light most of all). Cause: the remastered sun chroma is linear, while Classic applies its art-directed sunset colour (LightSun colorFull) in display space, so Classic's 7-degree sun shows red/blue near 2.9 on screen against an effective ~1.5 here. Below 16 degrees (in full by about 7) the rig's sun now takes 0.65 of Classic's sunset hue, taken to linear (EveningSunChroma). The full hue overshot into copper, because Classic's blue ambient cools its own sunlit side. Lab golden hour: the sunlit APC hull went from red/blue 1.54 to 2.06 against Classic's 1.99 (testview) and 1.56 to 2.19 against 2.29 (closeup); 14 degrees and above are unchanged, so the olive textures do not go mustard."
       - "2026-10-18: reviewed bug fixes landed on the branch (each red without its fix, green with it): capture rig pins object detail, settles each mode and resets lighting knobs, and setDate syncs street lamps like skipTime (874638c); NaN crown normals from zero leaf-card normals (d57b712); shadow-map unit 2 always holds a complete depth array, so NVIDIA 131204/131222 are gone (f102499); no cloud shadows under a clear sky, mean-preserving fade-in to overcast 0.11 (5cf85cf); sun shafts scaled by the air in front of each pixel, which removes the grey veil on near vehicles and also the warm near-ground beam (463506f); instanced runs keep each member's own terrain fit, a stock bug that shows once instancing runs (d80f868); switchLight on a non-lamp no longer crashes, StreetLamp had no casting id (ab61aa5); script-spawned vehicles get vertex buffers and the remastered lighting, crew views excepted (747ffc8); the night takes Classic's 1.0 local-light clamp and a real moon (4515770); three-entry config colours read as {r,g,b}, so lamps get their warm colour and 0.1 ambient, a data fix that also changes Classic and night vision near towns, committed alone (72f32d4). Not landed: object shadows at start-up (the patch also applied the terrain grid tier at boot, which changes physical terrain) and the 4x MSAA default (its migration also added MSAA on top of chosen supersampling). Full capture set 20261018-bugfix vs 20261017-final: all 26 modes settled, no GL warnings, town_night Remastered ground 157 -> 121 (Classic 120), lowsun_fp and sinai_lowsun_fp vehicles solid instead of veiled, coastline_sunset shore cloud shadow gone, Classic firefight ground darker near the Abel lamps (wash gone)."
